# custom_offsets.csv - your own hand-picked offsets/labels.
#
# Pass this file as the 2nd argument to build_all.sh and its entries get
# compiled into the GUI's "Custom Offsets" menu, separate from whatever
# build_all.sh auto-extracted from your BIOS into "Known Offsets".
#
# Simplest format - just an offset and a label (store defaults to "Setup",
# size defaults to 1 byte):
#
#   0x495,above 4g decode
#
# You can also give the store name and/or size explicitly:
#
#   Setup,0x495,1,above 4g decode
#
# Lines starting with # are comments and are ignored. One entry per line.
# Offsets are hex (0x...). This is exactly the format you'd get by reading
# the "VarOffset"/"VarStoreInfo" value out of a *.uefi.ifr.txt file that
# IFRExtractor-RS produced (see README.md), or anywhere else you found a
# documented offset for your board (forums, other tools' notes, etc.)

0x495,above 4g decode
